WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.669
Film Courage: When you write a first draft,
how detailed is that first draft?

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:05.770
Shawn Christensen co-writer/director of THE
VANISHING OF SIDNEY HALL Movie: How detailed…what

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:06.770
do you mean how detailed?

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:11.599
Film Courage: Well I know you talked about
previously off-camera you will go back over

00:00:11.599 --> 00:00:15.990
something fairly soon but when you are first
writing, when you are creating this world,

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:23.580
when you’re sitting down how much are you
getting into the details of the characters

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:29.349
and really thinking about their backstory
or are you just kind of putting out a structure

00:00:29.349 --> 00:00:32.520
(I know you don’t outline) of the story?

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.740
How much are you paying attention to certain
things?

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.560
Or are you just getting words out first?

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.800
Shawn Christensen: Well it depends on which
script.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.820
It depends on where the story is coming from.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:51.690
Generally speaking I don’t have a backstory
beyond a sentence or two.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:56.600
I don’t know what they were like in 6th
grade or anything like that.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:02.120
I just kind of take from people in real life
or combine people in real life or think of

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.120
people I know.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:11.220
And again, I just balance these characters
off each other knowing that this one is sort

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:16.220
of feisty and this one is sort of mellow and
this one is sort of this and then you can

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:22.310
add on the second or the third adjective sort
of as you go but I think in the beginning

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:30.710
if I’m going to introduce a character that
I’ve never written in my life and I say

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:38.300
Joe, 25, persistent…I don’t know, I’ll
say two adjectives and then I’ll just move

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.300
forward.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.300
That’s it.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.670
It’s real, real quick.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:47.000
And then I don’t necessarily have to deliver
on those adjectives if I feel like it’s

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.400
going in another direction, maybe he’s not
persistent?

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.050
Maybe he’s lackluster?

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:52.390
Maybe he’s lazy?

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.409
I don’t know.

00:01:54.409 --> 00:01:56.190
I have to like write him out a little bit.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:02:00.750
I have to let him talk in order to know.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:06.160
But the dynamic between characters is important
and the chemistry so I always start there,

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.870
that’s where I start.

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:12.230
And the story and the concept that I have
is like a sentence.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.190
It’s not an outline.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:16.890
That’s not detailed or in-depth.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:27.490
The first draft will be detailed to the extent
it needs to be in order to be concise, to

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:34.380
the point, and not dragging anywhere where
we don’t need to be in particularly in the

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.950
action.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:41.610
So when we enter this room, am I going to
tell you that it’s got blue walls and a

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:42.610
couch?

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:43.610
No.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:49.330
Because the characters are more important
and the room is for the director, it’s not

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.760
my job, I’m screenwriter.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.790
The room is for the director to decide.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:03:00.030
If you’re the director and the screenwriter,
great or whatever but people respond to characters

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.570
first and foremost.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:05.050
And so that’s just really the most detailed
part of my screenplay.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:09.870
I would say is the action is the briefest
part of my script.

